\section{Part 5: report}
At most 5 pages, with figures and tables from Parts 1--4. Answer, using mechanisms rather than just numbers:
\begin{enumerate}[leftmargin=*]
  \item At recall 0.95, which index is fastest on each dataset? Does it change?
  \item Build time and memory per index. What PQ saves and what it gives up.
  \item What Parts 3 and 4 show, and when headline numbers mislead.
  \item For 150{,}000 vectors and for 10 million, with a 100\,ms budget per query and 16\,GB RAM: use ANN or exact? Which index and settings? Use the exact timings.
  \item Two ways the benchmark could mislead, and whether each was tested.
\end{enumerate}

\section{Ground rules}
FAISS and hnswlib are allowed for indexes. Recall function, timing and plots must be own code. One machine; report its specifications and library versions. Do not use the ann-benchmarks framework for experiments. Do not copy numbers from papers or other students.

